         then a "binned" Gauss-Hermite function is used.  If        HISTORY              binsize=0 then a "normal, unbinned" Gauss-Hermite          HISTORY              function is used.                                          HISTORY   X0       An additive x-offset.  This is only used to                  HISTORY              evaluate the GH parameters that vary globally              HISTORY              with X.                                                    HISTORY   Horder   The highest Hermite order, Horder=0 means                    HISTORY              only a constant term (i.e. only Gaussian).                 HISTORY              There are Horder Hermite coefficients (since we fix H0=1). HISTORY   Porder   This array gives the polynomial order for the                HISTORY              global variation (in X) of each LSF parameter.             HISTORY              That includes sigma and the Horder Hermite                 HISTORY              coefficients (starting with H1 because we fix H0=1)        HISTORY              There will be Porder[i]+1 coefficients for                 HISTORY              parameter i.                                               HISTORY   GHcoefs  The polynomial coefficients for sigma and the                HISTORY              Horder Hermite parameters.  There are Porder[i]+1          HISTORY              coefficients for parameter i.  The Hermite parameters      HISTORY              start with H1 since we fix H0=1.                           END                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         